From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:13:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netproxy: a run of reads that find no proxy is put off longer
 each time (#4169)

A read of the system's proxy that comes back without one - scutil
answering and no proxy set (the machine the report came from: PAC only,
HTTP/HTTPS/SOCKS all off, so the read is a success and nothing failed)
or failing outright - now widens the none window, twice each time, up
to failKeep, a minute; a read that finds a proxy ends the run, and the
next miss stands the none window again. On main the fork ran every 2
seconds on such a machine while requests flowed - more often than a
machine with a proxy set (every 15) forks - and the fork is what killed
the process there; at the cap it runs once a minute, 30 times less
often. A proxy that turns up after a short absence is still taken at
the old pace (#1518), and one that turns up on a machine long without
one within failKeep.

A read that fails keeps what it read before and holds nobody, as
before (#3421).

Fixes #4169

